---
import Shell from '../../../components/RceSpecShell.astro';
import data from '../../../../spec-src/rce/spec.json';
const ov = data.chapters[0];
import facts from '../../../data/rce-facts.json';
const total = data.examples.reduce((a: number, g: any) => a + g.items.length, 0);
---
<Shell title="RCE language specification" description="The RCE language specification as an interactive notebook: plain-language introductions, formal grammar and typing rules, and runnable example programs checked in the browser." current="">
  <h1>RCE language specification</h1>
  <div class="rs-bar">
    <button type="button" class="tts-btn" data-target="rs-ov" aria-pressed="false"><span aria-hidden="true">▶ </span><span class="tts-l">Listen to the overview</span></button>
    <span class="tts-status" role="status"></span>
  </div>
  <div id="rs-ov" class="tts-text rs-intro" set:html={ov.sections[0].html} />
  <p class="rs-prose"><strong>Which version this is.</strong> This notebook is specification draft {facts.spec_notebook_draft}, generated from commit <code>{data.commit}</code> of <a href="https://github.com/openIE-dev/rce">openIE-dev/rce</a>. Public <code>rce</code> main was read at <code>{facts.commit}</code> ({facts.read_on}), draft {facts.spec_document_draft}. {facts.spec_notebook_commit === data.commit ? 'The notebook was generated from that commit.' : `The notebook commit ${data.commit} is behind ${facts.commit}, so these chapters do not yet show that document.`} There is one language: the specification at one commit. A <code># rce-version:</code> line is a release label, not a choice of language (specification section 2.7). The standard library is built into the checker. The repository states theorems {facts.theorems_stated}, with {facts.lean_modules} Lean files directly in <code>spec/lean/RCE/</code> and {facts.examples_total} accepted example programs ({facts.examples_valid_top_level} at the top level of <code>spec/examples/</code> and {facts.examples_in_packages} in packages; {facts.reject_examples} syntax rejects, {facts.ill_typed_examples} ill-typed and {facts.inadmissible_examples} inadmissible programs are refused). This notebook lists the top-level programs. Where a chapter quotes a count from an earlier draft, such as the draft 0.5 grammar result in the overview, it describes that draft. Counts come from <code>src/data/rce-facts.json</code>. The Lean kernel audit was not rerun at this commit.</p>
  <h2>Chapters</h2>
  <p class="rs-prose">Read them in order. Each chapter opens in plain words, then gives the exact rules. Formal grammar and typing rules sit in cells you can open and close. Every code cell can be edited and run.</p>
  <ol class="rs-cards">
    {data.chapters.map((c: any) => (
      <li>
        <a href={`/rce/spec/${c.slug}/`}><span class="rs-num">{c.num}</span>{c.title}</a>
        <p>{c.question}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <h2>Programs and the reading record</h2>
  <ul class="rs-prose">
    <li><a href="/rce/spec/examples/">All {total} example programs</a>: the accepted ones, and every syntax reject, ill-typed and inadmissible program with its expected refusal.</li>
    <li><a href="/rce/spec/read-protocol/">Read protocol</a>: how a reader, human or AI agent, shows it read each chapter, using the chapter fingerprints and read-receipt questions.</li>
  </ul>
</Shell>
